## Purpose

Replace all-inclusive App Server planning context with a deterministic, digest-bound reference
manifest and narrowly allowlisted read-only retrieval so large plans can be prepared without
raising the global inline-context ceiling.

## Desired Outcome

App Server planning receives the smallest useful inline manifest, retrieves only named source
ranges through a bounded contract, records content-free evidence of what was read, and returns a
controlled insufficient-context result when its budgets cannot support a safe plan. The behavior
is equivalent on Linux and Windows and is released and verified on every configured production
lane.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Retrieval contract | A digest-bound allowlist exposes only declared regular files and ranges from an isolated snapshot | existing planning snapshot |
| Correctness and budgets | Per-read and cumulative limits, evidence, and controlled insufficient-context fallback are enforced | retrieval contract |
| Portable release | Focused, full, Linux, Windows, upgrade, CI, release, and production checks prove the exact candidate | both implementation workstreams |

## Readiness Gate Transfer

1. `G-RETRIEVAL-CONTRACT` — digest-bound manifest and allowlisted read-only retrieval with no
   unrestricted shell, network, or parent-directory access.
2. `G-CORRECTNESS-BUDGETS` — per-read and cumulative limits, retrieval evidence, controlled
   insufficient-context fallback, and successful planning beyond the inline cap.
3. `G-PORTABLE-RELEASE` — full validation, Linux and Windows qualification, exact release, all
   configured production lanes, and released behavior.

## Constraints

- Reuse the isolated focused snapshot and App Server orchestration path.
- Bind every reference to the manifest digest and reject undeclared, changed, non-regular, or
  escaping paths.
- Keep retrieval read-only, bounded, deterministic, and content-free in retained telemetry.
- Preserve the existing source binding, pre-mutation fallback, no-replay, and no-network contracts.
- Do not introduce a general retrieval service or cross-run summary cache.

## Program Shape

1. Build the reference manifest, allowlisted range reader, planning integration, and focused proof
   as a Work2 candidate.
2. Complete budget/fallback coverage, cross-platform qualification, release, production
   convergence, and recursive reconciliation through Work5.

## Completion Boundary

The map is complete only when all readiness gates are demonstrated by one released exact commit,
all configured production lanes converge immediately, and the campaign, roadmap, map, and Idea
outcomes are satisfied and reconciled.

